        <mxCell id="V19b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1" value="THE DELIVERABLE" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="22" width="378" x="1806" y="3460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="XCUT" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FAFAFA;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=10" value="CROSS-CUTTING&#xa;&#xa;EXECUTION ISOLATION   everything past the build gate runs in a container. Builds and test runs get network, because dependency resolution needs it. Agent-authored harnesses do NOT.&#xa;                      Memory and CPU caps, wall-clock timeout, workspace bind-mount, shared dependency cache. Repository code and agent code are both treated as untrusted.&#xa;&#xa;RESUME                every stage checkpoints on (runId, stage, key) with an idempotent MERGE. A retry must reuse its key, or name what it supersedes; a retry under a NEW key leaves the&#xa;                      old row outstanding forever and the stage can never read as complete.&#xa;&#xa;NOTES vs EVIDENCE     notes influence what an agent DOES; evidence determines what an agent may SAY. Notes carry note_ ids, findings_record requires ^ev_, so a note is structurally&#xa;                      uncitable. The note kinds are ENVIRONMENT, CONVENTION, DEAD_END, FIXTURE, with deliberately no kind for assertions about bugs.&#xa;&#xa;HANDLES               large objects never enter an agent&#39;s context. Tools return an opaque, content-derived handle and the agent queries through it. A journal on disk lets a handle be&#xa;                      rehydrated after a restart instead of recomputed." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="2160" x="40" y="3510" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
